WEB SOURCE SHAPE (read end-to-end — covenant #3)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
QuietHoursPage.tsx (48 LOC) is a thin wrapper: `usePageTitle('Quiet hours')` + a
`<PageContainer title subtitle copyLink>` whose children are `<AIQuietHoursSuggestion/>` (the Helix
"suggest a window" advisor) above `<QuietHoursPanel/>` (the server-backed quiet-hours / DnD schedule
editor). The page owns ONE piece of local state — `pendingSeed` (a `QuietHoursWindowInput | null`):
  - `handleApplyDraft(patch)` is passed to the advisor as `onApplyDraft` → sets `pendingSeed`.
  - `<QuietHoursPanel seedDraft={pendingSeed} onSeedConsumed={handleSeedConsumed}/>` consumes it once
    per identity change (a `useEffect` copies it into the panel's `draft` form, opening the add/edit
    form pre-filled), then fires `onSeedConsumed` → clears `pendingSeed` back to null.
This is the propose-only contract (page comment + ADR-015 §I8): the advisor only PRE-FILLS the panel
form; the panel's own Save button stays the sole write path.

The manifest record (apps/parity/parity-manifest.json id=page:notifications/QuietHours) extracts exactly
the page-level surface: NO dataSources, NO named panels, NO charts, NO maps, and the two i18n strings
`notifications.quietHours.subtitle` / `notifications.quietHours.title` (requiredCount=2). The advisor
body and the schedule-editor body are the *separately-shipped* parity units, already DONE in this repo:
  - shared-surfaces/AIQuietHoursSuggestion.*  (the SwiftUI parity of components/ai/AIQuietHoursSuggestion)
  - feature-views/QuietHoursPanel.*           (the SwiftUI parity of features/settings/components/QuietHoursPanel)
Faithful, non-narrowing parity (covenant #2/#5) therefore = reproduce the PageContainer chrome (title +
subtitle + copyLink) AND host BOTH real child surfaces AND wire the seed hand-off between them (DRY — no
re-implementation), driven by the page model. This is the identical structure the sibling
page:notifications/Channels (P7) used to host its NotificationChannelsView — followed verbatim here.

