--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SEED HAND-OFF (web pendingSeed / seedDraft / onSeedConsumed — covenant #2/#5)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web page threads `pendingSeed` from the advisor's `onApplyDraft` into the panel's `seedDraft`, then
clears it via `onSeedConsumed`. In SwiftUI both children bind to long-lived @Observable models held by
the page model, so the React state round-trip collapses into a direct callback: the advisor model's
`onApply: (QuietHoursWindowPatch) -> Void` (its built-in propose-only hand-off, web `onApplyDraft`) is
wired to `panel.seed(from:)`. `seed(from:)` reproduces the web panel's `seedDraft` useEffect — it opens
the panel's add/edit form pre-filled from the proposed window (enabled/start/end/timezone/weekdays/bypass)
and calls `recomputePhase()` so an open draft suppresses the empty state exactly as the web
`windows.length === 0 && !draft` ladder does. No `onSeedConsumed` bookkeeping is needed because the
callback fires once per "Apply to form" tap and mutates the shared model directly (no stale-seed re-apply
is possible). `seed(from:)` lives in this unit's allowed file and touches only same-module members of the
shipped QuietHoursModel (draft / validationError are `public internal(set)`; recomputePhase() is internal)
— the panel surface files are NOT edited (covenant #7).

