ROUTE HOSTING (navigation registration — an allowed file per the prompt)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The value-less AppRoute enum's `.notifications` host is owned by the alerts inbox, and
/notifications/quiet-hours is a sibling alerts surface. Mirroring the sibling ChannelsRouteRegistration
(same directory, same pattern), the native shell models it as a typed NavigationDestination: a host stack
adopts `.quietHoursDestination()` and pushes a `QuietHoursLink` to open it. No AppRoute enum widening is
needed — AppRouteParser already resolves /notifications/quiet-hours to `.notifications` via its generic
first-segment fallback (verified: the parser's explicit map has /notifications/{rules,audit,webhooks,
archived,inbox} and falls back on first segment "notifications" -> AppRoute.notifications for the rest,
exactly as the sibling Channels registration recorded). The copy-link share URL uses the canonical web
path "/notifications/quiet-hours" (a constant, not user-facing prose). Changes therefore stay entirely
within the allowed feature dir + catalog + ledger + this log (no Sources/App or TeslaSyncApp edit).

