    the model owns the two web i18n keys + the two child @Observable models + the share URL + the seed wire.
  - Panels: the web page has NO panels of its own (manifest declares none) — it is PageContainer chrome
    around the advisor + the schedule editor. Reproduced faithfully: header (title + subtitle + copyLink) +
    BOTH hosted real surfaces. AIQuietHoursSuggestion renders the Helix invite/streaming/proposal/stream-
    error/gate states; QuietHoursPanel renders the windows list, the add/edit form, the per-row toggle/
    delete, and the save/delete toast — reused, not re-implemented (DRY).
  - Charts/maps: none (web source has none) — N/A.
  - 3 data states: the page's own surface has NO API data source (manifest declares none — it renders from
    navigation/local state); each hosted surface owns + renders loading / empty / error (+ the orthogonal
    stale/offline connectivity axis) for its own sources — its own parity unit, reused not re-implemented.
    The page's three previews (Loaded / Empty / Error) drive the panel's content / empty / failed phases
    through the in-memory source; the advisor renders its resting invite card under the AI-on gate.
  - Live data / staleness: handled inside the hosted surfaces (their .stale/.offline freshness chip +
    banner + guarded one-shot auto-refresh, ADR-013).
  - i18n: the two visible page strings resolve from Localizable.xcstrings by the web key names
    (notifications.quietHours.title / .subtitle) via the model's LocalizedStringKey; English fallbacks =
    the web t(key, default) second argument verbatim (ADR-014). Zero hardcoded user-facing literals in the
    page; the hosted surfaces resolve their own keys through their P1/S10 facades.
  - Units: the seed/window scalars (HH:MM local times, IANA timezone, weekday bitmask, bypass severities)
    are wall-clock schedule metadata, not SI physical quantities — no SI converter boundary is exercised on
    this surface (consistent with the shipped QuietHoursPanel unit).
  - a11y: header accessibilityElement(.contain); CopyLinkButton + both hosted surfaces carry their own
    labels/traits/VoiceOver summaries; Dynamic Type via Font.TS roles + .teslaSyncTheme(); light/dark +
    high-contrast via the Color.TS dynamic tokens; >=44pt controls from the shared TSButton (ADR-015).
    SwiftUI-native only — no WKWebView, no web cloning.
  - Adaptive: ScrollView + a centered max-width 1024 column (web PageContainer) that is regular on
    macOS/iPad and compact on iPhone; the hosted surfaces reflow their own content (ADR-002/006).

